  "Time-Dependent flow": {
    "type": "link",
    "typecategory": "Connectors",
    "description": "Time-Dependent flow",
    "icon": {
      "filename": "timedependent_flow.png"
    },
    "flow": {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "Flow rate",
      "includeinoutput": "true",
      "applylimit": "true",
      "ask_user": "true",
      "delegate": "Browser",
      "unit": "m^3/day;ft~^3/day;m^3/s;ft^~3/s"
    },
    "length": {
      "type": "value",
      "default": "1",
      "description": "Separation between the connected blocks",
      "helptext": "Distance between the centres of the two connected blocks. It divides the diffusive/dispersive exchange in Constituent::diffusive_masstransfer, so it must be the real separation or dispersion is scaled wrongly: a chain of 0.0254 m cells left at the default 1 m disperses 39x too weakly, and a dispersivity calibrated that way absorbs the error. The default of 1 m is kept only so existing models are unchanged -- set it for any model where dispersion or diffusion matters.",
      "ask_user": "true",
      "delegate": "UnitBox",
      "unit": "m;ft",
      "includeinoutput": "true"
    },
    "area": {
      "type": "value",
      "default": "0.000000001",
      "description": "Cross-sectional area of the connection",
      "helptext": "Flow area shared by the two blocks. It multiplies the molecular-diffusion term in Constituent::diffusive_masstransfer, so the default of 1e-9 m^2 suppresses diffusion entirely no matter what diffusion_coefficient is set on the constituent. Set it to the real interface area for any model where molecular diffusion matters. The tiny default is kept so existing models are unchanged.",
